A||||26||Gold-86SE||Chrysler PT Cruiser||||11||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||09:53 AM||||<BR>Guys, wondering if you have been watching the events unfold regarding the PT Cruiser from Chrysler?<P>Seems like these are selling like hot cakes and Chrysler is going up on its prices.  <P>People are waiting for months to get one of these things, kinda reminds of what I've read regarding the Fiero.<P>But this thing is small it is **168.8" long, which is 5" shorter than the Ford Focus or the Dodge Neon, but base line comes with a 5-speed manual 2.4L 4-cyl with 150 HP, all starting at 16K**, oh and add an extra 2-3K for the high demand.<P>Seems like a rather small vehicle to me, but sounds like it will scoot with 150 horses, that's better than the V6 Fiero, just forget about that deep rumble sound.<P>Would you by it?  I might in a year or two.<P>NOTE - **Data from USAToday**<BR>Check out the article here is the link, if it does not show properly as a hyper link, cut and paste to your browser:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.usatoday.com/news/acovtue.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usatoday.com/news/acovtue.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||05-16-2000||10:59 AM||||I've been thinking about one for a daily driver. (2 kids and a dog I could use the room) The Cruiser has 1 cubic foot less storage space than a Jeep Gran Cherokee! On Ebay there are about 15 for auction. People are buying them and auctioning them off! The auction prices are misleading. You'll see a Cruiser going for $5000. But if you read the ad this is OVER the $21,000 someone paid for it! (vehicle cost and tax) I just went thru AutoByTel to see what price they'll give me. (haven't heard back yet) If they want MSRP or more they can kiss my a$$. I bought my wife her 1998 Durango in 1998 when everyone kept telling me the dealers wanted MSRP or higher. I went thru AutoByTell and got it for $4000 less than MSRP.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-16-2000||11:10 AM||||I just heard back from the dealer I was suppose to contact. Here's there B.S. response:<BR>"Thank you for Submitting a request for a 2001 Chrysler PT Cruiser, to <BR>Autobytel. At this point, we will sell PT Cruisers, on <BR>a factory order basis, for manufacturers suggested retail price plus <BR>$2,000 for Limited Editions,and manufacturers <BR>suggested retail price plus $1,000 for Base and Touring Editions. We <BR>need a $1,000 deposit, which would be 100% <BR>refundable, if, at some future date, you decided not to complete the <BR>order. Anticipated delivery date at this time, <BR>according to information that Chrysler has given to us, could range <BR>anywhere from January, 2001 to April , 2001."<P>What a crock of Bat Guianno!!! Guess I'll keep my Saturn daily driver and fly past PT Cruisers in my Fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||11:22 AM||||<BR>I can't imagine having to wait almost 1 year to receive your ordered vehicle, what crock-o-crap, give me a break.<P>It also looks like Chrysler has become greedy based on the information given, wanting up to 2k more just because the demand is high. I don't recall ever reading anything like that regarding Pontiac and the Fiero.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||frontal lobe||05-16-2000||11:33 AM||||I'm not a Daimler/Chrysler apologist, but it's the dealers that get greedy in these situations.  I actually thank Chrysler for putting the car out for a retail price LESS than the market is willing to bear.  What something is worth isn't what some manufacturer puts as a price, it's worth what someone is willing to pay for it.  I guess right now, the public puts it worth higher than msrp.<P>I can remember when this happened with the Miata.||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||05-16-2000||12:13 PM||||Those PT Cruisers kick *SS! What blows my mind, is that my Dad, a die hard Camry lovin' import driver is planning on trading in his Camry for one. I give Chrysler alot of credit for having the kajones for producing cars like this. Fat chance you'll ever see something like this roll of GM assembly line in our lifetimes!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||05-16-2000||12:15 PM||||frontal lobe is right... it's the dealers, not the manufacturer that are trying to take advantage of the situation. Paying extra to order something is one of the biggest scams going. Dealers have to pay interest on their inventory. If a car is sold before it arrives it saves them a ton of money over one that sits for 6 months before it is sold.<P>They are a interesting looking vehicle though. I would consider one if I was in the market for that type of vehicle (and I could find a dealer that was reasonable).||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||12:32 PM||||Okay, so I have been corrected, that is fine, I can accept that I was mistaken/wrong.<P>However, I still think it is a crying shame for anyone to demand a higher price just because you place an order.  Give me a freaking break.<P>Taking an order for a car is not the same thing as auctioning the car.  Auctioning is asking people to state their highest price they are willing to pay.<P>Now, if the dealers were selling the cars to the highest payer/bidder that would be a completely different story, and btw fine with me - sell it to the person who is willing to pay more.  But give me a break charging people for an order - that is highway robbery.<P>missed a word - no matter how many times i read it, i still miss something.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||05-16-2000||01:14 PM||||Oh oh.  Gold-86SE, I wasn't trying to come across as correcting, so if I did I'm really sorry.<P>I'm not saying I disagree with you that it's a shame what the dealer's do.  I remember when the Mazda dealers did that when the Miata first came out, the manufacturer was TICKED.<P>What the dealers realize is if they don't add on the extra and take the extra profit, people will just buy the car even at msrp and turn around and sell it and take the profit.  I guess they figure they are entitled.  Ah, the price of being first in line!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||05-16-2000||01:23 PM||||That's okay. They can charge a $1-2K premium, if they want. But *I* won't be buying one. Wait 12-18 months. There will be incentives on these things, too. (There are also rumors of a Hi-Po drivetrain. Some sort of forced induction. Think they're going to keep it just for the Neon? Naaaahhh.) If Chrysler has any nads, they'll find a way to penalize the dealers who are inflating the prices. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||05-16-2000||01:46 PM||||I just remembered I live about 20 miles away from the factory that makes them! Has anyone ever bought a vehicle straight from the factory? Do I get to deduct the "destination" Charge since it's right outside the door of the factory?||||reg||3
Z||000011||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||02:11 PM||||<BR>Frontal, was not try to sound sassy, I was only letting everyone know that I can admit that I was uninformed and made a rash statement that had not been thoroughly thought out.<P>I did not take your comment personally(sp) please don't think that I was trying to climb don't your thought.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierosound||05-16-2000||08:31 PM||||The PT Cruiser is a cool looking car and the darling of the car industry because it the the "flavor of the month".  A couple months ago it was the Honda S2000.  In 1984, FIEROs were also the darling of the industry and Car Magazines when first introduced.  <P>This month, terms like "endearing styling", "cool retro coupe", "selling like hotcakes", "innovative design", "classic features" etc.  will be in every article reviewing the car. <P>By next year, its shorcomings will also be published in the very same magazines drooling over it today.  "Serious lack of power", "boulevard cruiser handling",  "poor Neon platform", "awkward rear visibility" etc. will be other descriptions being bandied about.  The car magazine industry does that to every NEW car it sees.<P>Don't get me wrong, I like the looks of the car, but it may still have some problems.  The 100,000 people who bought the 1984 Fieros found that out.  NEVER buy a car in it's INTRODUCTORY YEAR!!!<P><BR>I may want one in a couple years, a convertible, with 16" wheels, turbo charger option and rumble seat   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||14
