Z||000017||2M4 Dale||05-17-2000||10:19 AM||||If it don't have a GM badge on it somewhere I don't want it !!! I just wish GM would steal a couple of Chrysler styling/design engineers and come up with something COOL. (Like the Fiero - only NOT a rehash called a Fiero or maybe a Fiero that was truly a continuation of our little beasts)A new GTO...retro looks, rear drive and plenty of power would be good ! Chrysler don't have the sole rights to retro. I think retro is a great idea ! SO C'MON GM GET OFF YOUR BACKSIDES !!! Kill the Firebird/Camaro allready and come up with something new/old ??? ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Raydar||05-17-2000||10:29 AM||||A few months back, Car and Driver had an issue that covered one of the major auto shows. (Chicago? Maybe?) The cover story was a retro looking pickup-roadster that GM is rumored to be seriously considering building. It is an open 2-seater styled like a convertible 53 Chevy pickup, but it is *not* intended to be used as a truck. The prototype has an LS1 V-8. According to the article, interest in the project exceeded GM's wildest dreams. Rumor(?) has it being released in 2001-2002.<BR>Interesting.||||reg||1
